th/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>COCl</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>CONH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>CN</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f562ee0e063d926ccae"}, {"id": "047144", "text": "<p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Ffe0c7206-ef1a-4b0e-b963-717d1a7df809-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 284px; height: 55px;\" /></p>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f562ee0e063d926ccaf"}, {"id": "f1a0e8", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>COOH</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>COOR</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>CONH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>COCl</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f562ee0e063d926ccb0"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f562ee0e063d926ccb1", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfaf4"], "topics": ["60e5678e499d1e49588f927d"], "concepts": ["60e567c3499d1e49588f9946"], "question": {"text": "For the Compounds :\n(A) \\(\\mathrm{H}_3 \\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{CH}_2-\\mathrm{O}-\\mathrm{CH}_2-\\mathrm{CH}_2-\\mathrm{CH}_3\\)\n(B) \\(\\mathrm{H}_3 \\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{CH}_2^2-\\mathrm{CH}_2-\\mathrm{CH}_2-\\mathrm{CH}_3\\)\n(C) <img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fda5nvlYr1CIhuE3HoUe6xh-jy9aJGaqxf5PzQZVmLFA.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br />(D)<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fv25OHCYOnWku4s3HETq76vociqZ6YZaQvMrSuFuQpFw.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br />The increasing order of boiling point is :\nChoose the correct answer from the options given below :"}, "options": [{"id": "f80eb9", "text": "\\(\\text { (D) }  < (\\text { C }) < (\\text { A }) < (\\text { B })\\)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f562ee0e063d926ccb2"}, {"id": "a38fa6", "text": "\\(\\text { (B) }  < \\text { (A) } < \\text { (C) } < \\text { (D) }\\)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f562ee0e063d926ccb3"}, {"id": "c24b11", "text": "\\(\\text { (A) }  < \\text { (B) } < \\text { (C) } < \\text { (D) }\\)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f562ee0e063d926ccb4"}, {"id": "84b926", "text": "\\(\\text { (B) }  < \\text { (A) } < \\text { (D) } < \\text { (C) }\\)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f562ee0e063d926ccb5"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f562ee0e063d926ccb6", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfaf4"], "topics": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5676"], "concepts": ["60e5671a499d1e49588f87db"], "question": {"text": "A solution of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>-</mo></math> chloroaniline, <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>-</mo></math> chlorophenol and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>-</mo></math> chlorobenzoic acid in ethyl acetate was extracted initially with a saturated solution of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> to give fraction <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> . The left over organic phase was extracted with dilute <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> solution to give fraction <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> . The final organic layer was labelled as fraction <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> . Fractions <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></math> contain respectively:"}, "options": [{"id": "827b0f", "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>-</mo></math> chlorobenzoic acid, <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>-</mo></math> chloroaniline and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>-</mo></math> chlorophenol", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f562ee0e063d926ccb7"}, {"id": "546637", "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>-</mo></math> chlorobenzoic acid, <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>-</mo></math> chlorophenol and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>-</mo></math> chloroaniline", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f562ee0e063d926ccb8"}, {"id": "2ef99b", "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>-</mo></math> chlorophenol, <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>-</mo></math> chlorobenzoic acid and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>-</mo></math> chloroanilinc", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f562ee0e063d926ccb9"}, {"id": "868e1d", "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>-</mo></math> chloroaniline, <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>-</mo></math> chlorobenzoic acid and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>-</mo></math> chlorophenol", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f562ee0e063d926ccba"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f562ee0e063d926ccbb", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfaf4"], "topics": ["60e56814499d1e49588fa3a9"], "concepts": ["6162fbac6ed13040ec851b1f"], "question": {"text": "Which one among the following resonating structures is not correct?"}, "options": [{"id": "cea9b4", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F81c9b9a8-13ec-43de-bb26-e0dde906ab1d-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 212px; height: 102px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69